{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-psa-72-1","title":"Psalms 72:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":72,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":72,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 David, praying for Solomon, shews the goodness and glory of his kingdom, and in type of Christ's kingdom 18 He blesses God.</p>\n<p>A.M. 2989. B.C. 1015. (Title.) A Psalm.This Psalm seems to have been composed by David in his last days, when he had set his beloved son on the throne. \"Then,\" says Calmet, \"transported with joy and gratitude, he addressed this Psalm to God, in which he prays Him to pour out His blessings on the young king, and upon the people. He then, wrapped up in a divine enthusiasm, ascends to a higher subject; and sings the glory of the Messiah, and the magnificence of his reign.\"</p>\n<p>for. or, of. 127:1; *title Give. 1Ki 1:39-53; 1Ch 22:12,13; 29:19; 2Ch 1:10; Isa 11:2; Joh 3:34 Heb 1:8,9 the king's. 1Ki 1:47,48; 2:1-4; Jer 23:5,6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-72-2","title":"Psalms 72:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":72,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":72,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>He shall. 12-14; 45:6,7; 1Ki 3:5-10; Isa 11:3-5; 32:1,17; Jer 33:15; Re 19:11 thy poor. 12:5; 82:3,4; Job 34:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-72-3","title":"Psalms 72:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":72,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":72,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>mountains. 16; Isa 32:16,17; 52:7; Eze 34:13,14; Joe 3:18 little. 65:12 by righteousness. 85:10,11; 96:11-13; 98:8,9; Da 9:24; 2Co 5:19-21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-72-4","title":"Psalms 72:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":72,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":72,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>He shall judge. 12-14; 109:31; Isa 11:4; Eze 34:15,16; Zec 11:7,11; Mt 11:5 break. 2:9; 94:5; Job 19:2; 34:24; Pr 20:26; Jer 51:20-23 the oppressor. Isa 9:4; 51:12,13; Da 2:34,35; Zec 9:8-10; Re 18:6-8,20,24; 19:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-72-5","title":"Psalms 72:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":72,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":72,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>They shall. 1Sa 12:18; 1Ki 3:28 as long. 7,17; 89:29,36,37; Isa 9:7; Da 2:44; 7:14,27; Lu 1:32,33 1Co 15:24,25; Eph 3:21; Re 11:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-72-6","title":"Psalms 72:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":72,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":72,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>like. De 32:2; 2Sa 23:4; Pr 16:15; 19:12; Isa 5:6; 14:3-5; Eze 34:23-26 Ho 6:3; 14:5-7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-72-7","title":"Psalms 72:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":72,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":72,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>In his days. 132:15-18; Isa 11:6-9; 32:3-8,15-20; 35:1-10; 54:11-17; 55:10-13 Isa 60:1,22; 61:3-6,10,11; Mal 4:2; Ac 4:32 abundance. 1Ki 4:25; 1Ch 22:8,9; Isa 2:4; 9:6,7; Da 2:44; Lu 1:33; 2:14 Eph 2:14-17 so long as the moon endureth. Heb. till there be no moon.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-72-8","title":"Psalms 72:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":72,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":72,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>He shall. 2:8; 80:11; 89:25,36; Ex 23:31; 1Ki 4:21-24; Zec 9:10; Re 11:15 the ends. 22:27,28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-72-9","title":"Psalms 72:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":72,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":72,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>They that. 1Ki 9:18,20,21; Isa 35:1,2 his enemies. 2:9; 21:8,9; 110:1,6; Lu 19:27 lick. Isa 49:23; Mic 7:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-72-10","title":"Psalms 72:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":72,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":72,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>45:12; 68:29; 1Ki 10:1,10,25; 2Ch 9:21; Isa 43:6; 49:7; 60:3,6,9 Mt 2:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-72-11","title":"Psalms 72:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":72,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":72,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>all kings. 2:10-12; 138:4,5; Isa 49:22,23; Re 11:15; 17:14; 21:24,26 all nations. 86:9; Isa 11:9; 54:5; Ro 11:25; Re 20:1-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-72-12","title":"Psalms 72:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":72,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":72,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>For. 4; 10:17; 82:3,4; 102:17,20; Job 29:12; Isa 41:17; Lu 4:18; 7:22 2Co 8:9; Heb 7:25; Re 3:17,18 him. Ec 4:1; Isa 63:4,5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-72-13","title":"Psalms 72:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":72,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":72,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>shall save. 109:31; Job 5:15,16; Eze 34:16; Mt 5:3; 18:11; Jas 2:5,6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-72-14","title":"Psalms 72:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":72,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":72,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>he shall. 25:22; 130:8; Ge 48:16; 2Sa 4:9; Lu 1:68-75; Tit 2:14 precious. 116:15; Mt 23:30-36; 1Th 2:15,16; Re 6:9-11; 17:6; 18:20-24; 19:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-72-15","title":"Psalms 72:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":72,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":72,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>And he. 21:4; Joh 11:25; 14:19; 1Jo 1:2; Re 1:18 to him. 1Ki 10:14; Mt 2:11 shall be given. Heb. one shall give. prayer. 19; 45:4; Mt 6:10; 21:9; Joh 16:23,24; 1Co 1:2,3; 2Co 13:14 1Th 3:11; 2Ti 4:22; Heb 10:19-22 daily. 2Ch 2:11,12; 9:1,4-8,23,24; Joh 5:23; Php 2:11; 2Pe 3:18; Jude 1:25 Re 1:5,6; 5:8-14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-72-16","title":"Psalms 72:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":72,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":72,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>There. Job 8:7; Isa 30:23; 32:15,20; Mt 13:31-33; Mr 16:15,16; Ac 1:15 Ac 2:41; 4:4; 1Co 3:6-9; Re 7:9 upon. Isa 2:2,3 the fruit. 92:12-14; Isa 29:17; 35:2; Ho 14:5-7 of the city. 6; 1Ki 4:20; Isa 44:3-5; Jer 33:22; Re 7:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-72-17","title":"Psalms 72:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":72,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":72,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>His name. 45:17; 89:36; Isa 7:14; Mt 1:21,23; Lu 1:31-33; Php 2:10 shall endure. Heb. shall be. his name, etc. Heb. shall beas a son to continue his father's name for ever. Eph 3:14; Col 1:3; 1Pe 1:3 men. Ge 12:3; 22:18; Ac 3:16; Ga 3:14; Eph 1:3 all nations. Jer 4:2; Lu 1:48; Re 15:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-72-18","title":"Psalms 72:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":72,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":72,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>Blessed. 41:13; 68:35; 106:48; 1Ch 29:10,20 who only. 77:14; 86:10; 136:4; Ex 15:11; Job 9:10; Da 4:2,3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-72-19","title":"Psalms 72:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":72,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":72,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>blessed. Ne 9:5; Re 5:13 and let. Nu 14:21; Isa 6:3; 11:9; Hab 2:14; Zec 14:9; Mal 1:11; Mt 6:10,13 Amen. 41:13; 89:52; Nu 5:22; 1Ki 1:36; Jer 28:6; Re 1:18; 22:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-72-20","title":"Psalms 72:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":72,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":72,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>The prayers.This was probably the last Psalm he ever wrote; and with it ends the second book of the Psalter.</p>\n<p>2Sa 23:1; Job 31:40; Jer 51:64; Lu 24:51</p>"}]}